  "text": "Three more, about many pipelines at once. Between pipelines, don't guess with a cron offset: it breaks the first night the upstream runs late. Use a sensor on its output, a trigger on the dataset it publishes, or one DAG if the two are tightly coupled. Monitor more than success: runtime, freshness, volume, quality pass rates, and the SLAs consumers see. Alert once, to the owning team, naming the table, partition and check, and don't page on retries that heal themselves. And make it observable: structured logs with run and partition IDs, lineage from source to dashboard, and run metadata, like rows, duration and check results, kept as data. Then a failure at two in the morning is one slice to rerun. All of these pipelines feed tables and dashboards. The newest ones feed AI systems. Next: pipelines for AI.",
